							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "Font families are left as pele wrote them: `monospace` stays `monospace`. Skia does not resolve it (on Windows the text comes out proportional), and it draws `sans-serif` in another, thinner face than a browser on Windows does (Arial). To use real fonts, map the generic names in the theme (a single font name each). `themes/gt-windows.json` in the repository does it for Windows: `monospace` becomes `Consolas` and `sans-serif` becomes `Arial`, and the examples of `Pele2svgExamples` use it there."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
